# Performance

Read `docs/POWER_BUDGET.md` for background work; inspect the affected implementation before optimizing.

- Measure the actual bottleneck and preserve behavior. Do not apply `memo`, `useMemo`, or `useCallback` to every list item, callback, or array operation.
- Use narrow Zustand selectors. Derived collections used as subscription snapshots need stable references when their inputs are unchanged; cache by all relevant input references or use the established selector helper.
- Preserve cache-first startup, route-level lazy loading, and existing list/scroll behavior. Virtualization is a measured design choice, not an item-count mandate.
- For realtime catch-up, watch repeated copies of growing collections. Any batching must preserve event order, cursor durability, and owner checks.
- Inspect current build output and Vite configuration for bundle limits; old size snapshots are not current budgets.
- Report measured evidence and untested runtime/browser scenarios separately from static checks.
